---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/foce/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Bonus Project: Mini Cyclone</h1>

        <h4>
          Difficulty&nbsp;&nbsp;
          <i class="si-star text-sn-green"></i>
        </h4>

        <h4 class="text-sn-theme">Optional &mdash; Extra Credit</h4>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <section id="objective">
          <h2>What This Is</h2>

          <p>
            A light races along the row. Hit the button when it is on the target
            LED. Miss, and it speeds up to mock you.
          </p>

          <p>
            The quickest bonus project here &mdash; it needs no new parts at all,
            just the five-LED array and one button you already had wired for
            Activity 2.8.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="needs">
          <h2>What You&#39;ll Need</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>The five-LED array from Activity 2.6</li>
            <li>One button, from <code>3V3</code> with <code>Pin.PULL_DOWN</code></li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="tasks">
          <h2>Build It</h2>

          <ol>
            <li><b>Race the light.</b> Move a single lit LED along the row and wrap around to the start when it reaches the end.</li>
            <li><b>Pick a target</b> at random and remember which position it is.</li>
            <li><b>Stop on the press</b> and work out which LED was lit at that moment.</li>
            <li><b>Compare the two positions.</b> Hit or miss?</li>
            <li><b>Speed up on a hit, slow down on a miss</b>, so the game finds the player&#39;s limit on its own.</li>
          </ol>

          <p>
            This is the project that needs positions rather than traversal. You
            cannot compare &quot;where the light is&quot; against &quot;where the
            target is&quot; without asking the list <i>which</i> LED, so{" "}
            <code>leds[i]</code> and the index <code>i</code> both matter here.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="sample-output">
          <h2>What Success Looks Like</h2>

          <pre class="bg-sn-darker p-3 rounded"><code>Target: LED 3
HIT!   speeding up
Target: LED 1
miss   slowing down
Target: LED 4
HIT!   speeding up</code></pre>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <section id="extend">
          <h2>Then Make It Yours</h2>

          <ul>
            <li>Flash the whole row on a hit</li>
            <li>Beep differently for a hit and a miss</li>
            <li>Play best-of-five and report a score</li>
            <li>Mark the target by flashing it before the round starts</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <h1
          class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
        >
          Commence Project
        </h1>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
